<title>USA: TABLE-SBC Communications unit issues debt.</title>
<headline>TABLE-SBC Communications unit issues debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche debt issue from Southwestern Bell Telephone, a unit of SBC Communications was priced Tuesday according to lead manager Goldman Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>BORROWER SOUTHWESTERN BELL TELEPHONE</p>
<p>AMT $250 MLN	 COUPON 6.625 PCT  MATURITY 7/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.746  FIRST PAY DATE 1/15/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA3   YIELD 6.66 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P AA	  SPREAD 40 BPS     CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	 COUPON 7.375 PCT  MATURITY 7/15/2027</p>
<p>TYPE DEBENTURES    ISS PRICE 99.555  FIRST PAY DATE 1/15/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA3   YIELD 7.412 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P AA	  SPREAD 80 BPS     CALLABLE NON-CALL TEN</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
</text>
